.TH std::inplace_vector::try_emplace_back 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::try_emplace_back \- std::inplace_vector::try_emplace_back

.SH Synopsis
template< class... Args >                              (since C++26)
constexpr pointer try_emplace_back( Args&&... args );

Conditionally appends an object of type T to the end of the container.

If size() == capacity() is true, there are no effects. Otherwise, appends
direct-non-list-initialized with std::forward<Args>(args)... object of type T.

No iterators or references are invalidated, except end(), which is invalidated if the
insertion occurs.

.SH Parameters

args         -         arguments to forward to the constructor of the element
.SH Type requirements
-
T must be EmplaceConstructible into inplace_vector from std::forward<Args>(args)....

.SH Return value

std::addressof(back()) if size() < capacity(), nullptr otherwise.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Exceptions

Any exception thrown by initialization of inserted element. If an exception is thrown for
any reason, this function has no effect (strong exception safety guarantee).

.SH Notes

 This section is incomplete
 Reason: Explain the purpose of this API.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <complex>
#include <inplace_vector>

int main()
{
    using namespace std::complex_literals;
    using C = std::complex<double>;
    using I = std::inplace_vector<C, 3>;
    auto v = I{1.0 + 2.0i, 3.0 + 4.0i};

    C* c = v.try_emplace_back(5.0, 6.0);
    assert(*c == 5.0 + 6.0i);
    assert((v == I{1.0 + 2.0i, 3.0 + 4.0i, 5.0 + 6.0i}));

    c = v.try_emplace_back(7.0, 8.0); // no space => no insertion
    assert(c == nullptr);
    assert((v == I{1.0 + 2.0i, 3.0 + 4.0i, 5.0 + 6.0i}));
}

